{"type":"text","text":"Done. Mapping sheet 1 for Super Mario Bros. World 1-1, first screen is complete and promoted.\n\n## Where I started\nThe game was in the **attract demo**, not gameplay — `$0770` (game_mode) read 0. Per the given facts I pressed Start, waited, pressed Start again and confirmed the transition: `$0770`=1, TIME 398, the WORLD 1-1 card drawn, small Mario standing on the left hill.\n\n## Small Mario (the metasprite)\n**Proof:** `list_sprites` on the frozen frame (`$00CE`=176, so the OAM box top is y=177). The engine lays the player out as a 2-wide × 4-tall 16×32 OAM box in sprite palette 4; for small Mario the top two rows are blank `$FC` filler and only the bottom 16×16 carries pixels:\n\n| screen (x,y) | CHR tile | offset from (40,177) | flip |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| (40,177) | `$FC` blank | (0,0) | — |\n| (48,177) | `$FC` blank | (8,0) | — |\n| (40,185) | `$FC` blank | (0,8) | — |\n| (48,185) | `$FC` blank | (8,8) | — |\n| (40,193) | `$3A` (tile 58) | (0,16) | — |\n| (48,193) | `$37` (tile 55) | (8,16) | — |\n| (40,201) | `$4F` (tile 79) | (0,24) | — |\n| (48,201) | `$4F` (tile 79) | (8,24) | h-flipped |\n\nRecorded as `small_mario` (type sprite, group mario, confidence 1).\n\n## Mario's colours (palette 4 = `$22,$16,$27,$18`)\nRecoloured **slot 1** `$16` → `$2C` cyan, stepped a frame, screenshot: the **cap and shirt turned cyan**, while the face pixel stayed orange — proving slot 1 *is* the red cap/shirt and not the skin. `clear_palette_overrides` restored `$16` (verified `get_pixel_color(45,204)` back to red).\n- slot 0 `$22` periwinkle — never drawn (sprite index 0 = transparent)\n- slot 1 `$16` red — cap and shirt\n- slot 2 `$27` orange — face/skin and hands\n- slot 3 `$18` olive-brown — hair, mustache, shoes\n\nRecorded as palette `4`.\n\n## The bush\n**Proof:** `get_region` object mode at (215,200) → background palette 0, slots 1/2/3, 740 connected pixels, bbox (184,192)–(246,207), CHR `$125/$135/$136/$137/$138`; `read_nametable` (0,21–31, row 24–25) pinned each tile's position. All five recorded as tiles on pattern table 1, group `bush`:\n\n| tile | name | placement |\n|---|---|---|\n| `$125` | bush body fill (solid lime green) | row 25, cols 24–29 |\n| `$135` | bush bottom-left end cap | row 25, col 23 |\n| `$138` | bush bottom-right end cap | row 25, col 30 |\n| `$136` | bush top bump A (outline on its right edge) | row 24, cols 24/26/28 |\n| `$137` | bush top bump B (outline on its left edge) | row 25→24, alternating cols 25/27/29 |\n\n## Wrap-up\n`promote_mappings` promoted all 7 discoveries (0 hypotheses skipped) — the file now holds 23 tiles, 7 palettes, 1 sprite, 26 addresses. The emulator is resumed and running."}
